er |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Q1: What is the core community problem addressed?** | *“In semi-urban areas and student neighborhoods around colleges, civic problems like recurring potholes, uncollected waste, and non-working streetlights cause accidents and hygiene hazards. Traditional complaint mechanisms lack transparency, so citizens don't know if their issue was received or when it will be fixed.”* |\n| **Q2: How does your solution protect citizen privacy?** | *“The portal avoids collecting or displaying private mobile numbers and house door numbers. Instead, it utilizes public landmarks (e.g., 'Opposite College Main Gate') and optional resident tags to ensure citizen safety on a public transparency board.”* |\n| **Q3: Which UN Sustainable Development Goals (SDG) does this map to?** | *“It maps directly to **SDG 11: Sustainable Cities and Communities** (Target 11.6: reducing municipal environmental impact and managing municipal waste) and **SDG 16: Strong Institutions** (promoting transparent, participatory, and responsive public governance).”* |\n| **Q4: What technical stack did you use?** | *“Frontend is built with **React 18** and bundled using **Vite.js** for high performance. Styling utilizes **Tailwind CSS** for a responsive mobile and desktop government-portal interface, with **LocalStorage** for data persistence.”* |\n\nYou can open `civic_portal.html` right now to explore the application and take screenshots for your 1BCP308 report.","thinking":"Created a complete standalone single-file web application matching the user's reference image. Also created a complete React + Vite modular project with all source code. Now verifying all requirements are fully addressed.\n\n\nExamining the created project structure to confirm it addresses all specified features, including issue reporting, tracking, and the visual design requirements. The presence of components for header, hero section, form, issues feed, and footer indicates the modular approach to the user interface. Checking the sample data and README to ensure alignment with the VTU project context and the Indian community theme.\n\n\n"}
